ok   at u = -1/4 the grade factors are 5/2, 3/2, 1/2; t = 1/k_N, e = k_(N+2)/k_N: 2/5, 3/5, 2/3, 1/3
ok   at u = 1/4 k_0 = 0: the one critical zero; at the other points no factor vanishes
ok   on all 64 divided sets the rule's step weights are the law's grade factors at u = -1/4, N = 5 - |L_S|
ok   divided sets: 32 even (3/5, 1/28); {n} and the five directions (3/5, -1/22); a direction and its complement (1/3, -1/6); three of six (-1, 1/2)   [{(1, 5, '3/5', '1/28'): 32, (-1, 3, '1/3', '-1/6'): 10, (-1, 1, '-1', '1/2'): 20, (-1, 5, '3/5', '-1/22'): 2}]
ok   one pair of directions on opposite sides g^2 = [-Phi(1)/(1 + Phi(1))]/4 = [-Phi(i)/(1 + Phi(i))]/6 = e_line^2/(k_C^2 - 1) = 1/72
ok   a = (1 - Phi(1))/8 = 5/38; chi_A = 1/(1 + Phi(i)) = 13/12; w_h = 3/13; chi_h = 30/169

== 5. Completion at long wavelength: the field equations of the four breakings
ok   the five directions less their mean: sum v_t = 0, sum v_t (x) v_t = 1 on R^4, v_a.v_b = delta_ab - 1/5
ok   Klein-Gordon: at u = 1/4 - eps^2 m^2/24 the law's operator is (eps^2/8)(m^2 - Delta) + O(eps^3)   [[np.float64(0.006948988882833107), np.float64(0.0006937032596397201)]]
ok   Dirac: one step U = e^(-ik g_j) e^(-i mu g_h) has U + U^dagger = 2 cos k cos mu, every eigenphase cos w = cos mu cos k
ok   in the chart Gamma^mu = sum_t v_t^mu g_t and g(m) = sum_t g_t/sqrt5 are five anticommuting directions: (Gamma.p + M g(m))^2 = p^2 + M^2
ok   Maxwell and Yang-Mills: d^2 log det(I - wA_-[e^(i theta)]) = -kappa(w) C^T C exactly, kappa(w) = 2w^4/(1 - 5w^2)^2
ok   kappa = 1/200 at the counting points (w = +-1/5) and 1/98 at the amplitude points (w = +-i/3)
ok   tr(g_h g_a g_b g_c g_d) = 4 eps_habcd (times the sign of the volume element)
ok   so(5) = so(4) + R^4 at h: the four rotations that move h close into the six that keep it, [R^4, R^4] in so(4)
ok   the curvature of the ten rotations split at h, F = R - e^e/l^2, in the epsilon contraction: eps(F^F) - eps(R^R) = -(4/l^2)(R - 6/l^2) vol: Lambda = 3/l^2   [(np.float64(-14.998747474225183), np.float64(-14.99874747422534))]

== 6. Completion with two sources: the couplings, and the numbers in front of the field terms
ok   the clock's five marks (0, 1, 2, 3, -1/Phi(1))/4: ten gaps of mean E_D = 2
  strong          alpha_s = k4/(k2 sqrt(k_C^2 - 1))           = 0.117851130198   (PDG 2024 0.1180(9))
  electromagnetic 1/alpha = N_2(1 - x)k0^2/(c_L k2^2)           = 137.035999177   (CODATA 2022 137.035999177(21))
  weak            G_F m_p^2 = (1 - 1/N_2) W_W/M^2              = 1.02682689e-05   (1.0268268e-5)
  gravity         alpha_G = [k0^(-k_C El) eta^(k_C E_H)]^2     = 5.90615249e-39   (CODATA 2022 5.90615(13)e-39)
ok   alpha_s = (1/72)^(1/2) = 0.117851
ok   1/alpha = 137.035999177
ok   G_F m_p^2 = 1.026827e-5
ok   alpha_G = W^2, W = (2/5)^48 (295/296)^9 = k0(-1/4)^(-48) eta^9
ok   a circulation theta on the links moves the leading zero: log 4u_c = |theta_cyc|^2/48 + O(theta^4), 48 = k_C El = 2(40 - 16)   [[np.float64(0.02083369839649285), np.float64(0.020833366185580647)]]
  the link phases against the field in units of the charge: int F^2 = 8 pi kappa alpha ||C theta||^2, 8 pi kappa alpha = 9.170124e-04 at the plane hk
  and at colour 8 pi kappa alpha_s = 3.022369e-02; in front of F^2 stands 1/(16 pi alpha) = 2.726245, in front of R 1/(16 pi G)

